    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d140">

                <pb facs="0339" n="243" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg243"/>

                <head>No. 119.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Dichman to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Colon, Aspinwall, United States of
                            Colombia</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-08-14"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 14, 1878</date>.
                        (Received August 23.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In order to furnish the Department as
                    speedily as possible with the information requested in the Department’s dispatch
                    No. 4 of the 26th ultimo, which I received before leaving the United States, I
                    herewith forward a copy of the Official Gazette (Diario Oficial), containing the
                    law of the Colombian Congress approving of the convention concluded between the
                    United States of Colombia and the International Interoceanic Canal Company, and
                    the decrees issued in accordance therewith. The paper and translation have been
                    kindly furnished to me by Mr. B. Mozley, the general superintendent of the
                    Panama Railroad Company, and the Pacific Mail Steamship Company.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>Very, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>ERNEST DICHMAN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
